<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eisleben</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lutherstadt Eisleben</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eisleben, officially Lutherstadt Eisleben, is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harz">Harz</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> was born there in 1483 and died there in 1546, and the houses of his birth and death are <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Sites</a>. The town belonged to the counts of Mansfeld and was for centuries a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> mining in the Mansfeld region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eisleben.jpg" alt="Eisleben" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frans Bosch · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lutherstadt_Eisleben_Markt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Martin Luther (1483–1546), a mining entrepreneur’s son from <b>Eisleben</b>, had abandoned the study of law in 1505 for the Augustinian friary at Erfurt.</blockquote><a href="/movement/protestant-reformation">Protestant Reformation · People</a></li><li><blockquote>A line of its last stanza is inscribed on a memorial at Osterhausen near <b>Eisleben</b> in Saxony-Anhalt that commemorates both the Peasants' War of 1525 and the land reform of 1945, which the memorial's designers saw as fulfilling the peasants' cause generations later.</blockquote><a href="/songs/wir-sind-des-geyers-schwarzer-haufen">Wir sind des Geyers schwarzer Haufen</a></li><li><blockquote>Martin Luther was born in nearby <b>Eisleben</b> in 1483 and grew up in Mansfeld, where his father ran smelters.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-mansfeld">County of Mansfeld</a></li></ul></section>
